  "question": {
    "text": "Let the image of the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></math> in the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> be the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">γ</mi><mo>)</mo></math>. Then which one of the following points lies on the line passing through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">γ</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and making angles <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis respectively and an acute angle with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo></math>axis?",
